# The program the compiler compiles (generated by `scripts/checker_prog.py`; do not edit)

`checkerProgI`: `checkerProg` with its leaves of at most 80 nodes inlined (one round of
`inlRound`, `ConAgua/Compiler/Inline.lean`), as a literal whose functions the kernel checked one
at a time (`ProgIPart0` … `ProgIPart11`). The whole-program checks of the compiled code
(`ProgNrt`, `ProgSkt`, `ProgWf`, the asm parts) read the literal. That it is the inliner's output
and that it refines `checkerProg` (`checkerProgI_refines`) is `Checker/ProgIRef.lean`.
-/

